Nocturne patch to @formatjs/intl-datetimeformat 7.8.1, applied by
scripts/build_intl.py to a staged copy; the vendored file stays as published.

The first DateTimeFormat of a realm parses every format of its calendar
(760 for English Gregorian, with 2,995 range patterns) although the format
matchers read only the fields of each skeleton. parseDateTimeSkeleton now
keeps those fields eager and processes a format's pattern, 12-hour pattern
and range patterns the first time one of them is read, as ordinary data
properties from then on. In the host QuickJS harness the first construction
went from 95 ms to 18 ms, and 1,861 option sets in en, ja, en-GB and
ja-JP-u-ca-japanese gave identical resolvedOptions, format, formatToParts,
formatRange and formatRangeToParts results.

